CORE
main.c

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* y is reachable: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
pointer handling for concurrency is unsound
--
A pointer that a thread executed later in symbolic execution writes to a
shared object is in the value set of the reader: the first assertion holds,
and the second one fails because the reader may see the pointer to y.
